        "src": "/influence/controlled_opposition/cia-1984-mars-chrono-trigger.md)",
        "alt": "` / `*.png` / `*.jpg`; prefer **published** `https://paradigmthreat.net/...` URLs (timeline art often lives under `https://paradigmthreat.net/files/timeline/media/...`). **Placement:** one image **after** the paragraph that introduces the topic (illustrate the **linked investigation**, not decorate every section). **Alt text:** name the **source lane** and **what the reader should see** (e.g. “Historical antibodies — timeline chapter,” “Call of Duty militainment — Krasinski operator arc”). **Do not** copy images into the article folder unless you are creating **new** art; **link** to the canonical file in its home directory. **Newsletter budget:** many large PNGs + hero can trigger Gmail clipping—prefer **fewer, well-placed** reuses over a gallery; see **Length → Newsletter / inbox check**. **Reference:** [`influence/controlled_opposition/cia-1984-mars-chrono-trigger.md`"
      },
      {
        "src": "https://support.substack.com/hc/en-us/articles/360038866571-Why-does-it-say-Post-too-long-in-the-post-editor).",
        "alt": "` hero or opening hook paragraph)—not a `##`, not `> **TL;DR:**`, not a date stamp. Use `**Last updated:**` once at the **end** (with optional attribution after it); do not duplicate `**Updated:**` under the lede. **Grep the article for `|`** — any pipe-table row means **rewrite as paragraphs** before Substack paste (see **Tables, lists, and catalog prose**). Run the **Verifiable externals pass** below on every ship.\n\n---\n\n## Length (Substack / email)\n\n**Authoritative ceiling (email, not Substack’s own word cap):** Substack states there is **no** word-count or length restriction on posts, but the editor can show **“Post too long for email”** when the **email** may be **clipped or truncated** in some inboxes—specifically citing **Gmail** truncating messages **over 102KB** (**serialized message size** in the inbox: HTML, images, embeds, tracking—not raw Markdown word count). You can still publish; readers may need **“View entire message.”** There is **no** reliable standalone **“Gmail word limit”**; clipping risk tracks **rendered email bytes**. Source: [Substack Support — *Why does it say “Post too long” in the post editor?*"
